WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
Clean water matters to orcas, even though orcas live in the ocean.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:10.500
Rain can wash litter, oil, and chemicals into streams.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:16.000
Pollution can harm salmon habitat and move through the food web.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.200
Southern Resident orcas rely heavily on Chinook salmon.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:28.400
When salmon habitat is cleaner and healthier, more salmon have a chance to grow and return, giving orcas more opportunities to find food.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:36.000
With an adult, keep litter out of drains, use less water, and turn off unused lights and screens. Never unplug essential appliances.
